# Architecture (next-dato)

Complements `web-excellence.mdc` and `security.mdc`. Full map: [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Allowed imports |
|-------|------|-----------------|
| Domain | `src/core/` | Other `core/` only — **no React, Next, or fetch** |
| Infrastructure | `src/infra/` | `core/`, Node APIs, Dato client — **no UI components** |
| Lib | `src/lib/` | `core/`, pure utilities — prefer no React |
| UI | `src/components/` | `lib/`, `constants/`, atoms → patterns |
| App | `src/app/` | All above; orchestrates pages and API |

## Import direction

- `app` → `components` → `lib` → `core`
- `infra` consumed from Server Components, route handlers, Server Actions — not from client components
- Never import `infra/` or `app/` from `core/`

## Naming

- CMS blocks: `{Name}Block` in `*-block.tsx` or `sections/`
- Option resolvers: `resolve{Name}Options()` in `src/lib/datocms/`
- Image/link fragments: reuse `IMAGE_BLOCK_RESPONSIVE`, `LINK_HERO_CTA_FIELDS` in `queries.ts`
- Tests: colocated `*.test.ts` next to the module under test

## Change discipline

- Match existing patterns before introducing new abstractions
- Minimize diff scope — no drive-by refactors
- Register ST blocks only in `structured-text-block-view.tsx`
- Document defaults in resolver file header when CMS has `advanced_options` toggles

## Anti-patterns

- Business logic in `app/**/page.tsx` beyond fetch + compose
- Fetching DatoCMS inside client components
- Duplicating CMS field reads without `readCdaBool/String/Array`
- Hand-editing `src/infra/datocms/generated/**`
